# Student Management and Grading System

## Project Overview
Student Management and Grading System is a system that allows the user to manage students grades and perform operations such as adding, removing, searching, 
sorting, and printing student records. The system asks the user to input the student names and grades so that it will perform operations on the grades then displays students records.

## Setup  Instructions
-Python 3.10 or newer
-No external libraries are needed
-Run the program: python main.py

## Files
Files                     | what it does
Assignment Section A      |enters students and their grades, calculates average
Section B Assignment      |stores the grades as a tuple
SECTION C                 |stores the students in a dictionary
ASSIGNMENT SECTION D      |breaks the program into functions

## Features list
-validates grades entered by the user, values accepted are between 0 and 100
- Asks the user whether they want to display all students.
- Allows the user to search for a particular student by using their name.
- Allows the user to remove a student
- Allows a new student to be added
- Allows the user to update a grade for a specified subject.

##Class  Architecture 
The Student class represents a single student. each student is stored in a dictionary where the subject is a key and the grade is a value. This dictionary allows the student to have more than 1 grade for a subject.
methods
- valigatee grades: checks if the grades falls within the 0 and 100 grade. if it does not it raises an InvalidGradeError.
-add grades:validates the given grade and store it under the subject name in the list. if the subject does not exist, it creates alist fr=or that subject.
-calculate average: uses the values the values from the ductionary to calculate the average. If the the student has no grades, it will raise an Error for division bu 0.
-display students: prints the students with theu grade for subjects and their overall average.

The Gradebook class manages the whole class of students. It allows   add,  remove,  and  search  for  students and sorting the students.
methods
-add_student(student): adds a student to the dictionary. If the student already exists, it will reject the student
-remove_student(name) : removes the student from the dictionary. If the student does not exist in the dictionary, it will print an error message.
-search_student(name): searches a student in the dictionary by using their name.  If the student does not exist in the dictionary, it will print an error message.
-sort_by_average() : sorts students by using their average, from highest to the lowest.
-sort_students_by_name() : sorts students by alphabetical order.

